# preset-2card.args — `vllm serve` flags of the 2-card preset, 0.32.0-b70.5 (tensor parallel 2 + expert parallel, DFlash2 K=7 with the
# draft at TP2, 4 slots, 64 GiB host-RAM KV tier, 262,144-token context, sparse attention by default). It uses two cards so the other
# pair stays free for any other model. One flag and its value per line. Pair with preset-2card.env (cards, hot/cold expert offload) and a
# serve dir whose config.json is serve-config-qsa.json (sparse, the default) or ../../../v0.30/engines/serve-config-intel-autoround.json (dense);
# every other capability is a parameter, see meta.md "Parameters". The flags are the ones measured on 2026-10-26 (fork tag
# v0.32.0-b70.4); the .env adds the async hot/cold swap and BACKSTEP=0 (b70.5, numbers in meta.md "Presets").
# Run: v0.32/engine/serve.sh qwen38-flash-next preset-2card (v0.32/README.md "Build and run").
--served-model-name qwen38-flash-next
--host 0.0.0.0
--port 8000
--dtype bfloat16
--tensor-parallel-size 2
--enable-expert-parallel
--trust-remote-code
# 0.88 leaves too little KV for one 262,144-token request on this stack; 0.89 is the highest value vLLM's start-up
# free-memory check accepts on compute-runtime 26.35.
# PARAMETER gpu-memory: 0.89 measured; see meta.md Parameters
--gpu-memory-utilization 0.89
# the full context: hot/cold (145 cold experts per layer per rank, preset-2card.env) frees the VRAM for it
--max-model-len 262144
# prefill chunk 4096 tokens: +45-50 % prefill against 1024; 8192 bought nothing and cost 15 % KV
--max-num-batched-tokens 4096
# 4 concurrent sequences (2 is the fallback if preemptions show under load).
# PARAMETER slots: 4. Keep the capture list a multiple of 1+K = 8 up to slots x 8.
--max-num-seqs 4
--limit-mm-per-prompt {"image":2,"video":0}
# FULL graphs for uniform decode, piecewise for the rest. Capture sizes are every multiple of 1+K = 8 (K = 7 draft tokens)
# up to 4 x 8 = 32, so a uniform spec-decode step of 1..4 requests is never padded, plus three prefill sizes.
--compilation-config {"cudagraph_mode":"FULL_AND_PIECEWISE","cudagraph_capture_sizes":[1,8,16,24,32,256,512,1024]}
--cudagraph-metrics
--enable-auto-tool-choice
--tool-call-parser qwen3_xml
--reasoning-parser qwen3
# generic template (relative to the kit root; serve.sh runs there): the checkpoint's own template plus the thinking switch
# (off wins); behaviour and attribution belong to the client or gateway layer
--chat-template v0.32/models/qwen38-flash-next/chat_template.jinja
# server default temperature 0.7; a request's own value wins
--override-generation-config {"temperature": 0.7}
# when the per-effort thinking budget (B70_THINKING_BUDGET) runs out, close thinking with a short transition
--reasoning-config {"reasoning_end_str": "\n\nI have thought enough; time to answer.\n</think>\n\n"}
# CPU KV tier: 64 GiB in host RAM = 32 GiB pinned per rank (with B70_OFFLOAD_PRIVATE_PINNED=1 a private pool, no /dev/shm). About half
# the free host RAM goes to this engine; the rest stays for the model on the other pair (measured: 154.9 GiB MemAvailable at a 16 GiB
# tier, so about 107 GiB expected at 64 on our 256 GB host). Use 16 for a dev engine or with less RAM.
# PARAMETER KV offload size (GiB, host RAM; pinned, split evenly over the ranks): 64 on 2 cards (meta.md Parameters)
--kv-offloading-size 64
--kv-offloading-backend native
# DFlash2 block-diffusion drafter (incoai/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-DFlash2 @ a22a1744), 7 draft tokens, sharded over the
# 2 cards (draft_tensor_parallel_size 2; its KV page fits through patch 0038 of the sparse series); async scheduling stays on (the vLLM default), DFlash2 at K=7 only pays with it. The drafter runs on
# TRITON_ATTN; the target model takes vLLM's XPU default backend (FlashAttention), so no --attention-backend flag.
# PARAMETER drafter: DFlash2 K=7 (default). MTP: see meta.md Parameters
--speculative-config {"method":"dflash","model":"/models/qwen3.8-flash-next/DFlash2","num_speculative_tokens":7,"draft_tensor_parallel_size":2,"draft_sample_method":"probabilistic","rejection_sample_method":"standard","attention_backend":"TRITON_ATTN"}
# clients see cached prompt tokens in usage
--enable-prompt-tokens-details
